WEBVTT

NOTE
Captions for the GWTH.ai homepage explainer. Cue windows are word-aligned
to the final voiceover (VV7B fable100 take 005, 93.5s). British English,
no em dashes on screen.

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.740
Most people use ChatGPT like a search box.
Type a question, get an answer, move on.

2
00:00:06.980 --> 00:00:11.720
That works, but it barely scratches the surface
of what these tools can do.

3
00:00:12.520 --> 00:00:16.050
GWTH is an applied AI course for UK adults,

4
00:00:16.100 --> 00:00:20.480
built to take you from that first prompt
to serious, useful work.

5
00:00:20.760 --> 00:00:25.300
It runs for three months, about five hours a week,
in monthly parts.

6
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:31.340
It starts in plain English. No jargon,
and no coding needed to begin.

7
00:00:31.760 --> 00:00:35.920
Building comes later, and by the end
it is the spine of the course.

8
00:00:36.080 --> 00:00:40.040
You do not sit through theory.
You build small apps.

9
00:00:40.400 --> 00:00:43.200
You automate the jobs you repeat every week.

10
00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:47.400
You research faster,
and you make sense of your own data.

11
00:00:47.900 --> 00:00:52.630
Every lesson leaves real work behind,
evidence you can actually show,

12
00:00:52.680 --> 00:00:55.880
not a certificate that goes stale in a drawer.

13
00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:59.880
The credential is verifiable, and it stays current.

14
00:01:00.340 --> 00:01:06.640
We are independent. No sponsors,
no vendor deals, just what works.

15
00:01:06.860 --> 00:01:11.000
You can start free, with real labs and no card.

16
00:01:11.520 --> 00:01:15.420
If it suits you, course access is £29 a month,

17
00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:18.960
paid a month at a time,
and you can stop whenever you like.

18
00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.320
Here is the promise the whole course rests on.

19
00:01:22.680 --> 00:01:26.810
If you can describe what you want,
you can begin to build it.

20
00:01:26.860 --> 00:01:33.220
If that sounds like you,
come and take a look at gwth.ai.
